I go to the till with the green jacket and the yellow shirt.
Fortunately, the queue here is much shorter than in front of the fitting rooms.
It is my turn quickly.
The cashier greets me nicely.
"Good afternoon, did you find everything?" he asks.
"Yes, thank you," I answer and place the clothes on the counter.
He scans the jacket and the shirt.
"That comes to eighty-five Euro altogether," he says.
I pay with my card.
"Do you need the till receipt?" the cashier asks.
"Yes, please," I say quickly.
I did not try the shirt on, so perhaps I will still need it.
He gives me the till receipt.
I fold it and put it safely into my pocket.
Then I pack my new things neatly into the backpack.
"Thank you very much and have a nice weekend," the cashier says to me.
"Thank you, same to you!" I say goodbye.
I leave the shop and go to my bicycle.
I look forward to properly trying the clothes on at home.
